.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T22:08:12-07:00","id":1407445,"title":"","content":"I think all Tribes/Breeds have their GREATEST hero who is widely accepted, but I only remember several:<br /> <br /> 1. Silver Fangs: Sophia and Yuri Tvarivich who killed the Zmei<br /> 2. Silent Striders: Shu-Horus who almost killed Set<br /> 3. Children of Gaia: Lore-Speaker Gron?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T16:58:01-07:00","id":1407605,"title":"","content":"I keep a list of canon and novel shapeshifter characters. Are you looking for Garou or only Fera? I can't guarantee all of these are heroes because I've forgotten most of their stories, but I left out the ones I know are notorious for bad things.<br /> <br /> Ajaba: King Adeo (one of the first)<br /> <br /> Ananasi<ul><li>Abiele Dumont</li> <li>Anansi (a very great hero)</li> <li>Aracha Darkdweller (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Jericho Euler (taught humans to build cities)</li> <li>Limuloida (founded the Limul guards of Estotilandia)</li> </ul><br /> Bagheera<ul><li>Humbaba (discovered a new Gift)</li> <li>Tola</li> </ul><br /> Balam<ul><li>Blue Morning Skies</li> <li>Six Birds</li> </ul><br /> Bubasti<ul><li>Ananka</li> <li>Cymaa Ubastet (the first, or one of the first)</li> </ul><br /> Khan<ul><li>Sultan Jampal</li> <li>Sonn Bright-Kings</li> <li>Yu Kwan</li> </ul><br /> Pumonca<ul><li>Old Stone Face (a hero during the Wild West)</li> <li>Three Spiders Climb</li> </ul><br /> Qualmi<ul><li>Glowing Bundle Leap</li> <li>Moondaughter (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Strange Owl Woman</li> <li>Weeping Skunk</li> </ul><br /> Simba<ul><li>Abuja (first king of the Mor Grian, maybe also a Ceilican ancestor)</li> <li>Amandu (first Amandu'o king)</li> <li>Manu T\u2019Chaa</li> <li>Mayi (first Mayi'o king)</li> <li>Mountain-Stalker (one of the earliest)</li> <li>Plains-Lord (one of the earliest)</li> <li>Sakhmet (fought against Sutekh before he took over Khem)</li> <li>Taa Mlimba</li> </ul><br /> Swara<ul><li>Ayio Bon Parr (one of the earliest)</li> <li>Damaa (the first)</li> <li>Mana Ma Usaga</li> <li>Nyolo</li> </ul><br /> Corax<ul><li>Black Beak</li> <li>High Squeal</li> <li>Huginn and Munin (famous Norse Corax ancestors)</li> <li>Ice Feathers (Tengu)</li> <li>One White Feather (Tengu)</li> <li>Sharp Eyes (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> </ul><br /> Grondr: Brazentusk Mightyhoof (the last king)<br /> <br /> Gurahl<ul><li>Arturus the Bear King (= King Arthur)</li> <li>Chewanna First-Mother (one of the first)</li> <li>Goloy\u00e9 Seeks-After-Death (one of the first)</li> <li>Jessany Juniper-Eater</li> <li>Kari Woodsinger (one of the first Forest Walkers)</li> <li>Mountain Song (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Sedna Stalks-the-Glacier (one of the first Ice Stalkers)</li> <li>Slowfoot Groundshaker (one of the first Mountain Guardians)</li> <li>Yulia Finds-the-Way (one of the first River Keepers)</li> </ul><br /> Kitsune<ul><li>Bai Mianxi the White-Faced One (the first, and still alive)</li> <li>Fire-Splits-the-Sky (one of the first)</li> <li>Fukutenjin, the Celestial God of Good Fortune</li> </ul><br /> Gumagan<ul><li>Gadimargara</li> <li>Standing Stone (killed in the European invasion)</li> <li>Teeth-of-the-Kings (killed in the European invasion)</li> <li>Wolaru Radiant Light (famous hero, still alive)</li> </ul><br /> Mokole-Mbembe<ul><li>Dives Backwards (saved many Mokole and Bastet during 1st War of Rage)</li> <li>Liberation (U.S. Civil War hero)</li> <li>Light Between the Leaves</li> <li>Mokol\u00e9-Mbembe</li> <li>She Burns, Night\u2019s Fire (tortured in the 1st War of Rage, was driven mad)</li> <li>Oannes (taught humans some neolithic techologies)</li> <li>Two Thumbs (the first Mokole to gain a Homid form)</li> </ul><br /> Zhong Long<ul><li>Ao (an early Ao wereturtle)</li> <li>Meiying</li> </ul><br /> other and unspecified Mokole<ul><li>Joy-Hunter (Mesozoic)</li> <li>Sal-Afsan Far-Seer (Mesozoic astronomer)</li> <li>Sun Bright Scales (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Wave-Without-A-Shore (Mesozoic)</li> </ul><br /> Nagah<ul><li>Kala (one of the first)</li> <li>Mandrodari Ma</li> <li>Silent Striker (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Slippadikaram</li> <li>Takshaka</li> <li>Vasana the Three-Hooded, the Emerald, the Terrible (a great hero)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Nuwisha ancestors and Umbral Dansers<ul><li>Kokopelli Steals-the-Wind (Umbral Danser)</li> <li>Laughing Dream (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> <li>Old Man Manyskins, Laughing Manyskins (great hero, current Chosen of Coyote)</li> <li>Ptah Star-Rider (Umbral Danser)</li> <li>Weeps-With-Joy</li> </ul><br /> Ratkin<ul><li>Chagas Cruzi (recently killed hero; see the Ratkin opening comic)</li> <li>Scrounger (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)</li> </ul><br /> Rokea<ul><li>First-to-Fall</li> <li>Leaps-to-the-Wound (Oligocene, first friend of Remora)</li> <li>Sensei Mizuchi (the first Same-Bito - hero to some, traitor to others)</li> <li>Striking Tail</li> <li>Swims the Deep (hero before the Wars of Rage, in the PGttCB opening fiction)<